    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "20fe642f-c8d0-4c7a-a204-1fc7ad59c4b0",
      "cellIndex": 2,
      "originalCellId": "20fe642f-c8d0-4c7a-a204-1fc7ad59c4b0",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Hooke's law\nA spring has \n- $l_0$ _natural_ length, when no external forces are applied,\n- $l = l(t)$ the actual length at a given instant $t$.\n\nIf the spring is aligned in the direction set by vector $\\vec{r}$,\n$$\nF_\\mathrm{spring} = k (l - l_o) (- \\vec{r}) = k \\Delta l (- \\vec{r}) ,\n$$\nthe force is assumed to be linear with a factor called\n- $k$ spring constant.",
      "sourceSha256": "8201bea1dd61dfaa26502b7f71629bd4a9a8f737e6e77b176375244a5dd51a4c",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "l_0"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "l = l(t)"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "t"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\vec{r}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "display",
          "latex": "\nF_\\mathrm{spring} = k (l - l_o) (- \\vec{r}) = k \\Delta l (- \\vec{r}) ,\n"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "k"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "b3340b09-e412-40de-8a12-4c5d12195794",
      "cellIndex": 3,
      "originalCellId": "b3340b09-e412-40de-8a12-4c5d12195794",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Elastic potential energy\nIf the spring is displaced by $\\Delta l \\neq 0$ and released, it will return spontaneously to $\\Delta l \\neq 0$.\n\nAny work applied to the spring to bring it to this $\\Delta l \\neq 0$ is the same that will be **given back** by the spring with the opposite sign, because it will move in the opposite direction.\n\nThis is a distinctive property of a conservative force, therefore the potential energy satisfies\n$$\n\\vec{F} = - \\vec{\\nabla} V.\n$$\n\nIntegrating Hooke's law we find that the corresponding elastic potential energy is\n$$\nV_\\mathrm{spring} = \\frac{k}{2} (\\Delta l)^2 = \\frac{k}{2} (l - l_0)^2, \n$$\nwhere the sign of $(l - l_0)$ is not important because this factor is squared, and so $V_\\mathrm{spring}$ is always positive.",
      "sourceSha256": "98d4b2f601ce6979589ceb2da5b91dc09d1cd4a6923ada6ea3eddcb2b3afec10",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\Delta l \\neq 0"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\Delta l \\neq 0"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\Delta l \\neq 0"
        },
        {
          "kind": "display",
          "latex": "\n\\vec{F} = - \\vec{\\nabla} V.\n"
        },
        {
          "kind": "display",
          "latex": "\nV_\\mathrm{spring} = \\frac{k}{2} (\\Delta l)^2 = \\frac{k}{2} (l - l_0)^2, \n"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "(l - l_0)"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "V_\\mathrm{spring}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "284e8dd4",
      "cellIndex": 4,
      "originalCellId": "284e8dd4",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Example",
      "sourceSha256": "9bf34f44c9d1371f4eda569dfa04ff7830aff81cfa81646e680cef087714cdc1",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "63b207ae",
      "cellIndex": 5,
      "originalCellId": "63b207ae",
      "type": "code",
      "source": "import sympy as sm # import functions for symbolic manipulations\nfrom sympy.physics import mechanics as me # from sympy we use functions for mechanics\nme.init_vprinting() # dot notation for velocity and acceleration",
      "sourceSha256": "47cc9fd83cffe716d4bbead70b9c75481d194a8ce5f3eebc74e2dc4cf9fab241",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [
          "sympy",
          "sympy.physics"
        ],
        "calls": [
          "me.init_vprinting"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "4681a541",
      "cellIndex": 6,
      "originalCellId": "4681a541",
      "type": "code",
      "source": "m, k, omega, l, lo = sm.symbols('m, k, \\omega, \\ell, \\ell_o', positive=True) # system's parameters. The \\ell is a pretty l.\n\n# We define the generalized coordinates.\ne = me.ReferenceFrame('e') # frame of reference in cartesian coordinates\nt = sm.symbols('t') # time",
      "sourceSha256": "63f110192bead26d61e7ce4090955c8149771304688e4d4c97473c1cccd8a118",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "me.ReferenceFrame",
          "sm.symbols"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "408324c5",
      "cellIndex": 7,
      "originalCellId": "408324c5",
      "type": "code",
      "source": "particle_m = m\nparticle_r = l*e.x",
      "sourceSha256": "d0c1b2f70caec16aebfd1323c527efa1c75abc3743326e40201f7b8067428b5f",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "ffc4c959",
      "cellIndex": 8,
      "originalCellId": "ffc4c959",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "We declare the spring constant, the position of the free end and the condition for equilibrium.",
      "sourceSha256": "c27d1997c266ed4292e9a37c4490b03b4f923d6a64ebbe5e6aaae636daac8a8b",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "8284069c",
      "cellIndex": 9,
      "originalCellId": "8284069c",
      "type": "code",
      "source": "spring_rEquilibrium = lo*e.x # lo is the length at equilibrium (no external forces)\nspring_constant = k\nspring_r = particle_r # at the free end of the spring",
      "sourceSha256": "733d532105ffdd9b6de98bd83276f307e0c3eea46a840c22ee445b4d630a6f9e",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "b5571c62",
      "cellIndex": 10,
      "originalCellId": "b5571c62",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "The elastic potential energy in the spring is a function of squaring the __stretching__, or by how much is the free end displaced from the equilibrium. ",
      "sourceSha256": "da28a094bff0f6f20f702b07d2c351017ce0f6dc50ec20c05b2527a0a80ff990",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "b5c99fb4",
      "cellIndex": 11,
      "originalCellId": "b5c99fb4",
      "type": "code",
      "source": "stretching = spring_r - spring_rEquilibrium\nstretching",
      "sourceSha256": "9f94aa885073dc2eac690277f1aa81ad859140f9dee7651dc186d7c91bf6e2e4",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "(\\ell - \\ellₒ) e_x",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle (\\ell - \\ell_{o})\\mathbf{\\hat{e}_x}$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "0f33ea8f",
      "cellIndex": 12,
      "originalCellId": "0f33ea8f",
      "type": "code",
      "source": "(stretching).dot(stretching)",
      "sourceSha256": "21584c4c9da90a9e6e30162e583a058827a6e6885e47cd3464536315e96a06e5",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "              2\n(\\ell - \\ellₒ) ",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle \\left(\\ell - \\ell_{o}\\right)^{2}$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "stretching.dot"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "16027c6b",
      "cellIndex": 13,
      "originalCellId": "16027c6b",
      "type": "code",
      "source": "oneHalf = sm.Rational(1,2)\nstretching = spring_r - spring_rEquilibrium\nspring_V = sm.Eq(\n  sm.symbols('V_\\mathrm{spring}'),\n  oneHalf * spring_constant * (stretching).dot(stretching)\n)# elastic potential energy in the spring\nspring_V",
      "sourceSha256": "a19087d4f3de14e783a57d8e01570252a030267051415e61256f625875a25b36",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "                                    2\n                    k⋅(\\ell - \\ellₒ) \nV_\\mathrm{spring} = ─────────────────\n                            2        ",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle V_\\mathrm{spring} = \\frac{k \\left(\\ell - \\ell_{o}\\right)^{2}}{2}$"
        }
      ],
